# Production-Ready Blog System Documentation

## Overview

This document outlines the complete production-ready blog functionality system built for SEDS Pakistan. The system provides a robust, reliable, and fully controllable blog management solution through a comprehensive backend API and modern frontend interface.

## Architecture

### Backend Architecture

The blog system uses a **RESTful API architecture** built on Next.js API routes, providing:

- **Decoupled Frontend/Backend**: All blog content is managed via database and served through RESTful APIs
- **Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)**: Integrated with existing organizational roles
- **Scalable Database Design**: Uses Firestore for flexible document storage
- **Error Handling**: Comprehensive error handling and logging
- **SEO Optimization**: Built-in meta tag generation and URL optimization

### Frontend Architecture

- **Modern React Components**: Built with TypeScript and modern React patterns
- **Responsive Design**: Mobile-first design using Tailwind CSS
- **Real-time Updates**: Optimistic updates and proper loading states
- **Error Boundaries**: Graceful error handling throughout the application
- **Progressive Enhancement**: Works with and without JavaScript

## API Endpoints

### Public Endpoints

#### GET /api/blogs
Retrieve a paginated list of all published blog posts.

**Parameters:**
- `page` (number, default: 1) - Page number for pagination
- `limit` (number, default: 10, max: 50) - Number of posts per page
- `category` (string) - Filter by category ID
- `author` (string) - Filter by author ID
- `search` (string) - Search term for text content

**Response:**
```json
{
  "blogs": [/* EmorationalBlogPost[] */],
  "pagination": {
    "page": 1,
    "limit": 10,
    "hasNextPage": true,
    "total": 25
  }
}
```

#### GET /api/blogs/latest
Get the most recent blog posts for homepage display.

**Parameters:**
- `limit` (number, default: 3, max: 20) - Number of posts to return

**Response:**
```json
{
  "blogs": [/* EmorationalBlogPost[] */],
  "count": 3
}
```

#### GET /api/blogs/[slug]
Fetch a single blog post by its unique slug.

**Response:**
```json
{
  "blog": /* EmorationalBlogPost */
}
```

#### GET /api/authors
Retrieve a list of all authors and their post counts.

**Parameters:**
- `id` (string) - Get specific author with their posts

**Response:**
```json
{
  "authors": [
    {
      "id": "author_id",
      "name": "Author Name",
      "postCount": 5,
      "lastPostDate": "2024-01-15T00:00:00Z"
    }
  ],
  "totalCount": 10
}
```

#### GET /api/categories
Retrieve all blog categories with post counts.

**Parameters:**
- `includeCounts` (boolean) - Include post counts in response

**Response:**
```json
{
  "categories": [
    {
      "id": "category_id",
      "name": "Category Name",
      "postCount": 12,
      "slug": "category-slug"
    }
  ],
  "totalCount": 5
}
```

### Admin Endpoints

#### POST /api/blogs
Create a new blog post (requires admin/editor role).

**Request Body:**
```json
{
  "title": "Blog Post Title",
  "slug": "blog-post-slug",
  "content": "Full content of the blog post",
  "summary": "Brief summary",
  "thumbnailUrl": "https://example.com/image.jpg",
  "authorId": "user_id",
  "authorName": "Author Name",
  "categoryId": "category_id",
  "status": "draft|pending_review|published",
  "tags": ["tag1", "tag2"],
  "metaTitle": "SEO Title",
  "metaDescription": "SEO Description",
  "keywords": "keyword1, keyword2",
  "newsArticleUrl": "https://example.com/news",
  "publishDate": "2024-01-15T00:00:00Z",
  "unpublishDate": "2024-12-31T23:59:59Z"
}
```

#### PUT /api/admin/blogs/[id]
Update an existing blog post (requires admin/editor role or author ownership).

#### DELETE /api/admin/blogs/[id]
Delete a blog post (requires admin/editor role or author ownership). Performs soft delete.

## Data Models

### EmorationalBlogPost
```typescript
interface EmorationalBlogPost {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  body: string;
  authorUid: string;
  authorName: string;
  published: boolean;
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
  publishedAt?: Date;
  tags?: string[];
  
  // Enhanced metadata
  thumbnailUrl?: string;
  summary?: string;
  slug?: string;
  metaTitle?: string;
  metaDescription?: string;
  keywords?: string;
  newsArticleUrl?: string;
  status: 'draft' | 'pending_review' | 'published';
  categoryId?: string;
  
  // Emorational component data
  launchReadiness?: {
    verificationMetrics: VerificationMetric[];
  };
  dataShowcase?: {
    technicalSpecs: TechnicalSpec[];
    engineeringSeal: EngineeringSeal;
  };
  authorProfile?: AuthorProfile;
  analogArchive?: {
    documents: ArchiveDocument[];
  };
  futureHorizons?: {
    horizons: FutureHorizon[];
    primaryAction?: { text: string; url: string; };
    secondaryAction?: { text: string; url: string; };
  };
}
```

### User Roles and Permissions

The blog system integrates with the existing organizational role hierarchy:

#### Role Hierarchy for Blog Management
- **Blog Administrator**: Full control (superadmin, president)
- **Blog Editor**: Can publish, edit, delete any post (vice_president, general_secretary, advisor)
- **Blog Author**: Can create, edit, publish, delete own posts (projects_director, marketing_head, chairs)
- **Blog Contributor**: Can write and save drafts only (member)

#### Permission Matrix
| Role | Create | Edit Own | Edit Others | Publish | Delete | Manage Categories |
|------|--------|----------|-------------|---------|---------|-------------------|
| Admin | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
| Editor | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |
| Author | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ |
| Contributor | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ | ❌ |

